# --- Project-specific: large/raw data and model artifacts ---
# Raw source dataset is large and reproducibly downloadable; not committed.
data/raw/
# Trained model binaries are reproducible via `python -m src.models.train`
# and kept out of git history to avoid bloating it; small JSON result/metric
# files (e.g. comparison_results.json) ARE committed since they document
# actual results and cost nothing. Exception: final_model.joblib (the one
# Phase 5 actually selected, 617KB) IS committed - it's what Phase 7's API
# loads, and a fresh checkout/CI run should be able to serve predictions
# without first re-running the full training pipeline.
models_saved/*.joblib
models_saved/*.pkl
!models_saved/final_model.joblib
!models_saved/.gitkeep

# Prediction logs written by the API at runtime (not source-controlled).
logs/
*.log

# --- Secrets ---
.env
*.pem

# --- Terraform (Phase 10) ---
# State files can contain sensitive resource details (ARNs, IDs) and must
# never be committed, especially to a public repo. .terraform/ is a large,
# locally-downloaded provider plugin cache. .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed
# (Terraform's own recommendation, for reproducible provider version pins).
terraform/.terraform/
terraform/terraform.tfstate
terraform/terraform.tfstate.backup
terraform/*.tfvars
terraform/*.tfvars.json
